From: Shammah Chancellor <shammah.chancellor@notvalid.com>
Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 18:42:41 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] miner: don't read a backlog entry after popping it

BlockAssembler::addTxs took a reference to backlog.front(), popped the
queue, then returned a copy made through that reference, reading an
element pop() had already destroyed. AddressSanitizer reports this as a
container-overflow in miner_tests. Move the entry out before popping.

Coordinator integration provenance (reference405):
Preserve earlier purposeful source repairs through downstream consumer/context adaptations; exact conflict ledger retained.
All60 authored input payloads retained, with prerequisite-aware same-purpose splits; distinct legacy-index and inherited CXX compatibility remain independent. Pre-format source equals exact403+all60 control tree95718fceff83364b74294a751bd752b2f1a4e384. Only pinnedRuff import/format cleanup follows. Original author commands/hashes are historical reference evidence, not combined405 approval. Reference OFF/native/Rust full gates are preserved separately; combined compile/runtime NOT_RUN.

diff --git a/src/node/miner.cpp b/src/node/miner.cpp
index 3deb54925eaae2540d74817d57a2e5796bc403f3..7fdf1eefa1eeb774912bca49416d121d4dc10db3 100644
--- a/src/node/miner.cpp
+++ b/src/node/miner.cpp
@@ -373,7 +373,8 @@ void BlockAssembler::addTxs(const CTxMemPool &mempool) {
             return *mi++;
         }
 
-        auto &entry = backlog.front();
+        // Move the entry out before pop() destroys it.
+        CTxMemPoolEntryRef entry = std::move(backlog.front());
         backlog.pop();
 
         isFromBacklog = true;
